  {
   "type": "p",
   "html": "An FD provides a predetermined interest rate for the selected tenure, subject to the applicable terms. However, the interest rate is only one factor to consider before opening a deposit. Tenure, liquidity needs, premature-withdrawal rules, taxation and deposit insurance are also relevant."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "html": "The FD tenure should match when you expect to need the money, while the applicable rate and withdrawal terms should be checked before booking the deposit."
